I want to escalate a pattern before it turns into a bigger queue. We have 6 complaints about range dropping below 40 km in cold weather. Five of the six come from riders in the Netherlands, and four of them bought in the last two months.

The riders describe the same thing. They charge the bike fully at home in the evening, ride to work in the morning when it is around freezing, and the displayed range falls much faster than they expected. Two of them have already asked for a refund, and I have offered them the replacement check instead of a refund, since the bikes are not faulty as far as we can tell from the diagnostics.

I have attached the ticket numbers in a list below. I did not change anything on the tickets yet, so you can decide how we answer them as a group.

What I need from you is a decision on two things. First, whether we send one shared reply to all six riders explaining how cold weather affects the battery, or answer each one separately. Second, whether Engineering should see this as a range question or as a battery question. I would rather not guess on the second one.

I can take the calls on Monday if you want a shared script.

